<title>USA: U.S. power output slips 2.7 pct vs. year ago--EEI.</title>
<headline>U.S. power output slips 2.7 pct vs. year ago--EEI.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electricity deliveries in the continental U.S. totaled 60,151 gigawatt hours (GWh) for the week ended Dec 28, down 2.7 percent from the same period in 1995, the Edison Electric Institute (EEI) said.</p>
<p>The amount of weekly power supplied to the southeastern U.S. fell the most from a year ago, down 11.7 percent to 13,997 GWh, EEI said.</p>
<p>Year-to-date domestic power production totaled about 3.30 million GWh, up 2.3 percent from the same period in 1995, EEI said.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
